1
00:00:00,030 --> 00:00:02,460
A gecko could hang from your ceiling all day,

2
00:00:02,460 --> 00:00:03,870
with no glue at all.

3
00:00:04,010 --> 00:00:05,570
Look closer at its toes.

4
00:00:06,150 --> 00:00:07,500
They're lined with ridges,

5
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:10,030
covered in about two million tiny hairs.

6
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:13,390
Each hair splits into hundreds of even tinier tips.

7
00:00:13,700 --> 00:00:18,110
They're so small, they get close enough for the molecules themselves to pull together.

8
00:00:18,430 --> 00:00:22,210
A patch of hairs the size of a coin could lift a small child.

9
00:00:22,620 --> 00:00:25,980
To let go, a gecko simply peels its toes back,

10
00:00:25,980 --> 00:00:28,810
like tape, up to fifteen times a second.

11
00:00:29,090 --> 00:00:30,900
So if one ever lands on your ceiling,

12
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:32,320
don't wait for it to fall,

13
00:00:32,320 --> 00:00:32,767
because
